# figs

Scripts that draw the paper's figures from the result tables of `experiment-repo` (what each reads: `../docs/data_contract.md`).
Everything at once: `../make_all.sh RESULT_TABLES_DIR OUT_ROOT`. One figure: `python3 figN_*.py DATA_DIR OUT_PREFIX [options]`; each writes
`OUT_PREFIX.pdf`, `.csv` (the plotted numbers) and `.json` (input hashes, size, selection). Scripts fail when an input or column is missing; they never fill in values.

| Figure | Script | Claim |
|---|---|---|
| Fig 1 | `fig1_concept.py` | concept: one instance, runs against the exact values |
| Fig 2 | `fig2_headline.py` | M2, M3 (share vs budget, aggregate agreement, P_c distribution) |
| Fig 3 | `fig3_margin.py` | M4 |
| Fig 4 | `fig4_budget.py` | M5 (error vs m, paired estimator differences at equal evaluations, m* vs margin) |
| Fig 5 | `fig5_floors.py` | M6 |
| Fig 6 | `fig6_certificate.py` | R1 |
| Tables | `../tables/tab1_design.py` (1), `tab2_guidance.py` (2), `tab3_certificate.py` (3), `tabA1_sensitivity.py`, `tabA2_h1.py` | design, guidance, R1 budget rule, appendix |

Rev 6 (Outline): Fig 5 labels floor b "B=50" and draws open markers where fewer than K=10 retrained models were kept; Fig 6/Table 3 label the registered contrast and the matched-deliverable variant and give each Brier with its base rate; Table 2 says d is descriptive; every figure json carries the interval scope sentence. Fig 4c is secondary until the probit fit exists.

Not yet drawn: appendix A2 (background sensitivity: `background_sensitivity.csv` not delivered), the RF log-odds vs probability comparison of A1.
Sizes: NeurIPS 2026 text block 5.5 in; 7 pt ticks/legend, 8 pt labels, 6 pt sub/superscripts (`figstyle.py`, venue-repo#3: the venue states no floor, 7 pt is its recommendation). Fonts embedded as Type 42.

